/**
 * The [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) `justify-content` property defines
 * how the browser distributes space between and around content items along the `main axis` of a
 * flex container and the [inline
 * axis](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Logical_properties#inline_direction) of
 * grid and multicol containers.
 *
 * Initial: normal. Inherited: no.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Grammar: normal | <content-distribution> | <overflow-position>? [ <content-position> | left |
 * right ]
 *
 * Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-align-3/#propdef-justify-content
 *
 * Author guide:
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/justify-content
 *
 * Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
 *
 * Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
 *
 * Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.
 */
module std.css.properties.JustifyContent.

